<article class="env-lemma" id="042M">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/042M">Lemma <span data-tag="042M">67.10.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $j : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$j$ is a monomorphism (as in Definition <a href="/tag/042L" data-tag="042L">67.10.1</a>), 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$j$ is a monomorphism in the category of algebraic spaces over $S$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the diagonal morphism $\Delta _{X/Y} : X \to X \times _ Y X$ is an isomorphism. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that $X \times _ Y X$ is both the fibre product in the category of sheaves on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ and the fibre product in the category of algebraic spaces over $S$, see Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/02X2" data-tag="02X2">65.7.3</a>. The equivalence of (1) and (3) is a general characterization of injective maps of sheaves on any site. The equivalence of (2) and (3) is a characterization of monomorphisms in any category with fibre products. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>